Article 32

Social rehabilitation as referred to in Article 26 paragraph (1) letter number is a service provided by companions to restore the traumatic condition of victims.

(1 Social rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by: (2)
a. providing guidance and counseling;
b. psychological recovery of victims;
c. accompanying victims in the family and community environment; and d. providing Safe Houses for victims of violence who require ongoing treatment. Special social rehabilitation for women victims of domestic violence and trafficking in persons is carried out by: (3)a. providing guidance and counseling;
b. psychological recovery of victims;
c. accompanying victims in the family and community environment; d. providing skills training and education; and €. providing business capital assistance.

Social rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by Regional Apparatus having principal tasks and functions in the fields of: (4)
a. social affairs;
b. Cc.  d. women's empowerment and child protection; education health; ande. mental and spiritual.

In addition to being implemented by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (4), social rehabilitation may also be implemented by the community or social service institutions (5).

CHAPTER II PREVENTION OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN Part One Forms of Violence Against Women and Children Article

Forms of violence against women and children include:

a.
c. d.  f. physical violence;

psychological violence;

sexual violence; neglect;

exploitation; and/or other violence.

Article Physical violence as referred to in Article letter constitutes an act that results in pain accompanied by injury, wounds or disability to the body, miscarriage, fainting and/or causing death of women and/or children.

Article Psychological violence as referred to in Article letter constitutes an act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or psychological suffering of women and/or children. Article Sexual violence as referred to in Article letter includes: a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. coercion of unnatural or unwanted sexual relations; and/or c. coercion of sexual relations with others for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes.

CHAPTER VII

INVESTIGATION

Article 44

In addition to Investigation Officials of the State Police of the Republic of Indonesia, investigation of criminal acts referred to in (1) this Regional Regulation may be conducted by Civil Servant Officials within the Bengkalis Regency Government whose appointment is determined in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Civil Servant Investigators as referred to (2) in paragraph (1), are authorized to:
a. conduct examination of the validity of reports or information concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
b. conduct examination of any person and/or business entity suspected of participating in criminal acts related to violence against women and children in the business environment;
c. request information from any person and/or business entity in connection with criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
d. conduct examination of evidence, records, or other documents concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
e. conduct examination at certain places suspected of containing evidence;
f. conduct seizure of goods and materials resulting from violations that can be used as evidence in criminal cases related to violence against women and children;
g. request assistance of experts in the framework of carrying out investigation duties concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children; andh. terminate investigation if there is insufficient evidence of criminal acts related to violence against women and children.

In carrying out its authority, Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall coordinate with the Police in accordance with the provisions (3) of laws and regulations.

4. Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigation Official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.

Article 26

Forms of services to victims as referred to (1 in Article 24 letter b, are as follows:
a. services to women and children victims of acts of violence, include:
1. complaint, consultation and counseling services; accompaniment services;

health services;

legal aid services;

repatriation and social reintegration services; and 6. social rehabilitation services.
b. in addition to the forms of services regulated in letter special services are also provided which include: 1. pick-up services; and/or
2. medical and psychological referral services. Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter and letter b, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus (2) in accordance with minimum service standards established by the government.

Further provisions regarding the implementation of services (3) as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

