CHAPTER VII

INVESTIGATION

Article 44

In addition to Investigation Officials of the State Police of the Republic of Indonesia, investigation of criminal acts referred to in (1) this Regional Regulation may be conducted by Civil Servant Officials within the Bengkalis Regency Government whose appointment is determined in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Civil Servant Investigators as referred to (2) in paragraph (1), are authorized to:
a. conduct examination of the validity of reports or information concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
b. conduct examination of any person and/or business entity suspected of participating in criminal acts related to violence against women and children in the business environment;
c. request information from any person and/or business entity in connection with criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
d. conduct examination of evidence, records, or other documents concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
e. conduct examination at certain places suspected of containing evidence;
f. conduct seizure of goods and materials resulting from violations that can be used as evidence in criminal cases related to violence against women and children;
g. request assistance of experts in the framework of carrying out investigation duties concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children; andh. terminate investigation if there is insufficient evidence of criminal acts related to violence against women and children.

In carrying out its authority, Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall coordinate with the Police in accordance with the provisions (3) of laws and regulations.

4. Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigation Official of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.

Article 16

Women and children victims of acts of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 15, also receive special rights, as follows:
a. the right to respect and full use for survival, growth and development;

the right to basic services;

the right to equal protection;

the right to be free from various stigma;

the right to obtain freedom;

the right to obtain empowerment; and the right to be tried based on restorative justice.

Article 23

Prevention as referred to in Article 22 letter a, is implemented by: (1)
a. forming a network in efforts to prevent violence against women and children;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns; c. establishing a system for preventing violence against women and children;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence;
e. providing knowledge about prevention and mechanisms for handling violence against women and children; and f. enhancing the role and value of local wisdom and the role of custom in the protection of women and children. Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus that (2) have main duties and functions in the fields of: empowerment of women and protection of children; education;

health;

social affairs and manpower;

youth and sports; and
f. mental and spiritual.

Regional Apparatus in preventing acts of (3) violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1) may involve related agencies.

In addition to being implemented by Regional Apparatus and related agencies as referred to in paragraph (3), prevention (4) is also implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community, NGOs, universities, community organizations, social organizations and religious organizations; and c. business world.

Procedures for preventing acts of violence against women and (S) children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

Paragraph Services

Article 41, the Regional Government may partner with the business sector, NGOs/social organizations concerned with women and children in the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through: (2)
a. notification of employment opportunity information for women victims of violence;
b. education and training for women and children victims of violence;
c. educational assistance for women and children victims of violence who have been withdrawn from their education; d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of violence;
e. providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities, the private sector and various non-governmental organizations concerned with women and children from various forms of violence; and/org. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from various forms of violence up to the Village level.

Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is set forth in the form of an agreement in accordance with (3) the provisions of laws and regulations.

