Part Three Rights of Victims

Article 15

Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights: a. the right to be respected for their dignity as human beings; b. the right to recovery of health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims; the right to determine their own decisions;

the right to obtain information;

the right to confidentiality especially regarding their identity personality; the right to compensation;

the right to social rehabilitation;

the right to complaint handling;

the right to assistance; and i.
j. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process.

Article 16

Women and children victims of acts of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 15, also receive special rights, as follows:
a. the right to respect and full use for survival, growth and development;

the right to basic services;

the right to equal protection;

the right to be free from various stigma;

the right to obtain freedom;

the right to obtain empowerment; and the right to be tried based on restorative justice.

