a. women's empowerment and child protection; b. social affairs;
c. manpower;
d. health;
e. education;
f. security and public order; andg. mental and spiritual.

In carrying out duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1) Regional Apparatus may (3) cooperate with government agencies, provincial governments, other district/city governments and the community as well as the business sector.

