CHAPTER III PROVISION OF SERVICES FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE Part One General

Article 17

Protection of women and children is the shared responsibility of:
a. Regional Government;
b. Parents, Guardians and/or Family;
c. Community; andd. Business world/private sector.

REGENT OF BENGKALIS,

Considering that women and children have the right to obtain a sense of
a. security and freedom from acts of violence, exploitation and maltreatment as guaranteed in the 1945 Constitution;

that the implementation of protection of women and children is the authority of the Regional Government based on Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government; that in order to prevent and protect
c. women and children victims of violence, regulations are needed to guarantee the implementation of protection of women and children in the Region; that based on the considerations as referred tod. in letter a, letter and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;
